    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0738" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 800.61/18</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-03T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 3, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3023. Referring to your December 1, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d572-f1"/> sent
                    by Taylor for Secretary of Agriculture stating, “Can you appoint member on <pb
                        facs="0739" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/> commission to study production with
                    Allies? Must understand our export conditions in fertilizer, seeds and
                    machinery.” Secretary of Agriculture informs me that he is now ready to
                    designate representative of his Department for service on this commission, and
                    also two assistants, experts in their particular lines. You are instructed to
                    ascertain present status of this enterprise and report whether any changes in
                    the plans have been made and if it is still desirable for American
                    representatives to become members of this commission. Please cable when and
                    where these representatives if appointed should go.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
